  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership mapping and consultative workshop for Sierra Leone and Liberia Partners.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This workshop is to guide and inform CAFOD&#x2019;s future engagement and increase awareness of the organisations&#x2019; development and humanitarian interventions in Sierra Leone and Liberia. It is a strategic approach aiming to help CAFOD design quality programmes that will support the new thematic programme framework (participatory governance, food and livelihood security, EPPR, including WASH). The idea is part of the organisation&#x2019;s continuous shifting approach seeking to meet the dynamic needs and aspirations of people we work with.  Bringing together over 20 leading stakeholders across each of these countries, the workshop is designed as a mixed interactive session and hands-on group work that will inspire dialogue on the issues, driven by a human centred approach and facilitated by CAFOD programme team.</narrative>
  </description>
